From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:15:39 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Workbench agents survive closing its tab and come
 back after a restart with the same flags

Closing the Workbench tab no longer ends its terminals: they are kept by the
profile's Workbench service (output and exit buffered through a TermSink,
guard questions held until a Workbench takes the session back, Mission
Control keeps the session) and the next Workbench that opens the project
takes them back. After a restart, Codex sessions resume too (codex resume
<id>, its thread id from notify), and Claude Code keeps its model
(--model, from the status line's model.id) and Remote Control
(--remote-control).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
